{"title":"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be chosen at random from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. What is the probability that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9954af0afc226930c792cbc2e0668ef1fc1f7872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}4x\\rfloor - \\lfloor\\log_{10}x\\rfloor = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"19\" />?\nHere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the greatest integer that is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/086c22a6e12fd8a862c2c553dba0670d085718ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\frac 18 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac 3{20} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac 16 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac 15  \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"370\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be an arbitrary integer. For which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> do we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9ab95f789c6b50ebe31b2e923db5973738d88c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}4x\\rfloor = \\lfloor\\log_{10}x\\rfloor = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"19\" />?\n</p><p>The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4d2e3a674af7e0f0f24b6da1a238137faf57d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}x\\rfloor = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"19\" /> can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/5295da19eb2aa649b3708d9385b3d595e67a7050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^k \\leq x &lt; 10^{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />. The second one gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90d2b032d1babb94ef22f86ebf596b67fdf720f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^k \\leq 4x &lt; 10^{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />. Combining these, we get that both hold at the same time if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f53cc25e2458f5bf8f797866075ca1216f7f94d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^k \\leq x &lt; \\frac{10^{k+1}}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Hence for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we get an interval of values for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9954af0afc226930c792cbc2e0668ef1fc1f7872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}4x\\rfloor - \\lfloor\\log_{10}x\\rfloor = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"19\" />. These intervals are obviously pairwise disjoint.\n</p><p>For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23fa365b4a0751d7292384305fbca7fb7329316e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> the corresponding interval is disjoint with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, so it does not contribute to our answer. On the other hand, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b043119262a2beb49176cb4beb5c50ec1915a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> the entire interval is inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Hence our answer is the sum of the lengths of the intervals for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b043119262a2beb49176cb4beb5c50ec1915a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>For a fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> the length of the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47f27f00a17b2434ddf1a50a456d596a97cbd0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[ 10^k, \\frac{10^{k+1}}4 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"100\" height=\"44\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d35635182849bae8e118fc4b5205c8650697cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 32\\cdot 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"51\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>This means that our result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/66362d70547dfaf83aff31571d3591cd0ed58ff1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 32 \\left( 10^{-1} + 10^{-2} + \\cdots \\right) = \\frac 32 \\cdot \\frac 19 = \\boxed{\\frac 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"285\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad23c112010fbf57d3d35bb956c54b44a1d64c4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ecdf579f047118eed51c59652bb79fff813df60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 10^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fce809a49cf02d76de2cd32309546c0498e1918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}4x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> doesn't fulfill the condition unless <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8365ca24fc34a05a85b5b3c32d9049b4f96e81b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{-2} \\leq x &lt; 0.25 * 10^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" />. The same holds when you get smaller, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb55554c1b2f63a8a8c22789bdc07fa54bfbea83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0.25 * 10^{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e4f873107bffa06aff7bf154f25daac593cecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is the lowest value such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> becomes a higher power of 10.\n</p><p>Recognize that this is a geometric sequence. The probability of choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fce809a49cf02d76de2cd32309546c0498e1918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}4x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5d9273cd203ec290c30286a608c73e501ad347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" /> both equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472449a81b0591e71269e557b418e59fc8fc64fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9/10)* (15/90) =15/100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" />, because there is a 90 percent chance of choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ecdf579f047118eed51c59652bb79fff813df60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 10^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, and only values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0a382ce3d6bb1bb75ce59ed25bc26724c57450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca53097709d5ea8add7dae667d3b3a9dc709cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.25*10^{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> work in this case. Then, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fce809a49cf02d76de2cd32309546c0498e1918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}4x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5d9273cd203ec290c30286a608c73e501ad347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\log_{10}x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" /> both equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, you have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c9379131e057c61783373c44e7dd5e89603b0f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1/10) * ((9/10) *(15/90))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"18\" />. This is a geometric series with ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a3d67ed68c56765f7050e4a060eb6de5470dd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />. Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f5cb4536d71b01c01a8d04d369fbdb47b2f9224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/(1-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> for the sum of an infinite geometric sequence, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c85e1bc316449ee44c3cc453d2ead00508489a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(15/100)/(1-(1/10)) =  \\boxed{\\frac 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"222\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by Halt_CatchFire\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B\">2006 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017144647\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 342/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9318/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.979      1 -total\n 63.08%    8.818      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 35.40%    4.948      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2331:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017144647 and revision id 154069. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}